<title>GERMANY: Audi details Jan-Feb 1997 sales, profit.</title>
<headline>Audi details Jan-Feb 1997 sales, profit.</headline>
<text>
<p>First two months of 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group sales				  3,320   vs 2,880</p>
<p>    Group investment			   183     vs 182</p>
<p>    Group customer vehicle deliveries    89,368  vs 67,742</p>
<p>Of which</p>
<p>    -- Germany				   38,640  vs 29,121</p>
<p>-- Western Europe excluding Germany  37,431  vs 27,525</p>
<p>    -- United States			   4,852   vs 3,546</p>
<p>    -- Rest of World			   8,445   vs 7,550</p>
<p>    Group vehicle production		 88,262  vs 72,581</p>
<p>Of which</p>
<p>    -- A3					  20,853  vs 83</p>
<p>    -- A4/80				     47,746  vs 51,530</p>
<p>    -- Cabriolet				 1,240   vs 1,258</p>
<p>    -- A6/100				    15,819  vs 18,057</p>
<p>    -- A8					  2,604   vs 1,652</p>
<p>    Group average workday production     2,718   vs 1,872 cars</p>
<p>    Group workforce (28.2.97)		36,143  vs 33,502</p>
<p>Of which</p>
<p>    -- Audi AG				   34,939  vs 33,109</p>
<p>    -- Audi Hungaria Motor		   1,204   vs 393</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German carmaker is Audi AG, a unit of Volkswagen AG. Audi siad growth was recorded in virtually all key market.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
